n lux-seconds (daylight), as printed with bar notation (3.0 with an overbar = -3.0); the axis runs -3.0 to 1.0 and the curves are drawn from about -2.83 to 1.0.","log_h_ref is exactly as printed: the sheet prints 'Log H Ref: 0.84' with no minus sign, while the Gold 200 plot on the same page prints '-1.14'. A positive value would lie at the top end of the plotted range, so a lost minus sign (-0.84, which is 0.30 above Gold 200's -1.14, as expected for one stop less speed) is likely; not confirmed by the sheet. Check: the traced r density is 1.07 at -0.84 (inside the printed grey-card range 0.90 to 1.10) but 1.81 at +0.84.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/50 s, daylight, density 0.2 above D-min; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed, the axis runs 0.0 to 4.0. The cyan-forming (r) curve has a small blue hump (about 0.6 at 395 nm), then runs along the 0.0 baseline (hidden in the frame line, so about 470-485 nm is interpolated) before the red peak.","Spectral-dye-density plot has only 'Midscale Neutral' (mid) and 'Minimum Density' (min), no separate c/m/y dyes.","Printed checks (Status M red-filter densities of a normally exposed negative): grey card 0.90 to 1.10; lightest paper-gray-scale step 1.30 to 1.50.","Grain: Print Grain Index for 135 at 4x6 print (42); only that size is listed. The sheet says the film is optimized for printing on Kodak Ektacolor Edge Paper, Kodak Royal Digital Color Paper and Kodak Professional Endura Metallic Paper.","log_h_ref: the sheet prints \"0.84\" without its minus sign (Gold 200 on the same page prints -1.14); -0.84 is used, where the traced red density (1.07) lies inside the printed grey-card range."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":21.6,"grain_size":20.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}